  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vanuatu Australia Policing and Justice Program - Phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Vanuatu Australia Policing and Justice Program (VAPJP) Phase 3 aims to strengthen policing and justice services in Vanuatu so that all people, especially the most vulnerable, can access fair, equitable and high quality support that contributes to a safe and just society. Phase 3 focuses on two interconnected End of Program Outcomes: (1) the Vanuatu Police Force delivers inclusive, responsive and accountable services that enhance community safety; and (2) legal protections and justice services are inclusive and accessible, particularly for survivors of sexual and gender based violence. To achieve these outcomes, the program supports the Vanuatu Police Force and the Ministry of Justice, Youth and Community Services to work collaboratively across the justice continuum, from police response and victim support to prosecution and adjudication, to strengthen the sector as a whole.</narrative>
  </description>
